---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
---

<Legal title="Data deletion" description="How to delete your AdMobot data, including data received from Meta (Facebook, Instagram, Threads, ads), Google, LinkedIn, X and Pinterest." updated="12 October 2026">
  <p>You can remove your data from AdMobot at any time.</p>

  <h2>Disconnect a channel</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Open AdMobot and go to <strong>Automation Center → Connections</strong>.</li>
    <li>Choose the channel (for example Instagram, Facebook, Threads, LinkedIn, X, Pinterest or Google). For ad accounts, open <strong>Wallet</strong> and disconnect Meta Ads or Google Ads; for Google Analytics and Search Console, open <strong>Analytics</strong> and disconnect Google and click <strong>Disconnect</strong>.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>This deletes the channel's access token from our servers immediately and, where the platform allows it (Google, Meta Ads, X, LinkedIn), also revokes AdMobot's access there. AdMobot can no longer publish to it or read its data.</p>
  <p>
    You can also remove AdMobot from the platform itself: on Facebook and Instagram, open <strong>Settings → Apps and websites</strong> and remove AdMobot; on Threads, remove it under your Threads account's website permissions; on Google, open <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions">myaccount.google.com/permissions</a> and remove AdMobot; on LinkedIn, X and Pinterest, open your connected apps settings and revoke access.
  </p>

  <h2>Delete your whole account</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}?subject=Delete%20my%20AdMobot%20account`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a> from the address you signed up with, with the subject "Delete my AdMobot account". We delete your workspace, Brand Brain, posts, images, metrics and channel tokens within 30 days and confirm by email. Billing records we must keep by law are retained only for that purpose.
  </p>
</Legal>
